<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Open Notes – Pypi</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/pypi/</link><description>Recent content in Pypi on Open Notes</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sun, 01 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0530</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/tags/pypi/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>SynapC: Minimalist Neural Network Library in C</title><link>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/synapc/</link><pubDate>Sun, 01 Sep 2024 00:00:00 +0530</pubDate><guid>https://nagarajrpoojari.github.io/opennotes/projects/synapc/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/nagarajpoojari404/SynapC" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="https://pypi.org/project/synapc/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PyPI Package&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; · &lt;a href="#python-quickstart"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python Quickstart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SynapC&lt;/strong&gt; is a minimalist, dependency-free neural network library implemented entirely in pure C from scratch, featuring native Python C-extension bindings. It provides a transparent, low-overhead way to understand and execute feedforward neural networks (FFNN) and gradient-based backpropagation without relying on massive framework runtimes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="architectural-workflow"&gt;Architectural Workflow&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="architectural-workflow"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#architectural-workflow" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div role="img" aria-label="Diagram"&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid hx:mt-6"&gt;
flowchart LR
PythonApp[Python Application Code] --&amp;gt;|Python C-API / ctypes| Binding[SynapC Extension Layer]
subgraph CEngine [Pure C Core Engine]
Binding --&amp;gt; Alloc[Tensor &amp;amp; Layer Allocator]
Alloc --&amp;gt; Forward[Forward Pass: Matrix Multiply &amp;amp; Activations]
Forward --&amp;gt; Loss[Loss Computation: MSE / Cross-Entropy]
Loss --&amp;gt; Backward[Backward Pass: Analytical Gradients]
Backward --&amp;gt; Optimizer[SGD Optimizer &amp;amp; Weight Updates]
end
Optimizer --&amp;gt; Forward
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="key-features"&gt;Key Features&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="key-features"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#key-features" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pure C Engine&lt;/strong&gt;: Implemented from scratch using standard C runtime without external dependencies (no BLAS/LAPACK required).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python C-Extension&lt;/strong&gt;: Seamless Python API (&lt;code&gt;pip install synapc&lt;/code&gt;) exposing fast compiled C execution to Python workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customizable Topologies&lt;/strong&gt;: Arbitrary multi-layer feedforward neural networks with configurable layer dimensions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activation Functions&lt;/strong&gt;: Built-in support for Sigmoid, ReLU, Tanh, and Softmax activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Backpropagation&lt;/strong&gt;: Fully analytical gradient calculation and Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) weight updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
